'''Route 32''' (Japanese: '''３２ばんどうろ''' ''Route 32'') is a route in central [[Johto]] connecting [[Violet City]] and [[Union Cave]]. The eastern entrance to the [[Ruins of Alph]] lies at the route's northern end.

==Route description==
Route 32 begins with a small path leading away from Violet City, which splits into two. One path leads west, to the eastern entrance of the Ruins of Alph. The other path leads south to the rest of Route 32. The player cannot continue south of the intersection until they have obtained the {{pkmn|Egg}} from [[Professor Elm]]'s aide in Violet City.

The southern path begins with two large hills separated by a [[ledge]]. Going around the southern edge of the second hill will bring players to a [[Cuttable plant|cuttable tree]] on its western side, behind which is a path leading to a man who will give the player {{TM|05|Roar}}. 

From there, the path continues south, where it splits around another hill. The western path leads through [[tall grass]], while the eastern path leads past a {{pkmn|Trainer}}. These paths briefly join before splitting once more. Players can choose to follow the western path along the shoreline of the ocean, traveling through tall grass; or they can cross the ocean on the pier, where three [[Fisher (Trainer class)|Fishermen]] can be found. 

Shortly after the pier ends, the two paths rejoin and continue south. A [[Pokémon Center]] can be found near the end of the route, allowing players to heal their Pokémon before entering Union Cave. A man inside the Pokémon Center will give players an [[Old Rod]], and in [[Generation IV]], a fan of [[Kurt]] located in the Pokémon Center will give the player two [[Lure Ball]]s.

North of the Pokémon Center, [[Week Siblings|Frieda]] can be found on Fridays. She will give the player a [[Poison Barb]] the first time they meet her, and in Generation IV, she will give a {{DL|List of Ribbons in the games|Relax Ribbon}} all other times, provided the player has met each of her siblings. On days other than Friday, a [[Great Ball]] can be found where Frieda usually stands.

South of the Pokémon Center is a final Trainer. Directly west of this Trainer is the entrance to Union Cave.

In {{2v2|HeartGold|SoulSilver}}, the track for the [[Magnet Train]] can be seen crossing over the route near the sea.

